Module drove "The held drove" {
  Description "The Rì's customs-men at Porthalen hold Bran, the Brynach lead-drover: their clerk says forty head crossed the march-stone and thirty-six were shown for the toll. Bran says thirty-six crossed. His drove stands bawling in the pens, unsold, and his boy is minding them alone.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place town "The town" is settlement.
  Place green "The green" is room.
  Place taproom "The taproom" is room.
  Entity keeper: group "The innkeeper".
  Relation offstage(entity).
  Relation freed(group). Relation sent(group). Relation watered(group). Relation fined(group). Relation turned(group). Relation thanked(group). Relation counted(group).
  Relation sold(group). Relation cried(group). Relation bidden(group). Relation halved(group). Relation emptied(group). Relation paid(group). Relation gone(group). Relation heard(group). Relation told(group).

  Entity held: fact "The customs-men at {town} hold Bran, the Brynach lead-drover, for cheating the Rì's toll: four head short, their clerk says.".
  Initially Assert established(held).
  Entity clerk_count: fact "Mardle, the customs clerk: forty head crossed the march-stone.".
  Entity boy_count: fact "Owain: thirty-six crossed; four went into the Black Rhyne.".
  Entity bran_count: fact "Bran: thirty-six crossed, and Mardle has found other droves four short.".
  Entity altered: fact "In Mardle's tally-book the forty for Bran's drove is written over a thirty-six, in fresher ink.".
  Entity road_west: fact "The drove road goes west from {town} up the pass to Caer Brynach, where the lord pays for swords.".

  Place customs "the customs-house" is room within town at 6, 3.
  Place pens "the drove pens" is room within town at 6, 4.
  Place rhyne "the Black Rhyne, behind the pens" is room within town at 7, 4.
  Passage customs_door "the customs-house door" is door between green and customs.
  Passage pens_gate "the gate to the drove pens" is passage between green and pens.
  Passage rhyne_bank "the bank down to the rhyne" is passage between pens and rhyne.

  Observe held_sight at green as sign when not freed(party) "Across the green the customs-house door stands open, and a customs-man in the Rì's blue leans on the jamb with his staff. From the pens beyond comes the bawling of cattle nobody has fed." teaches held.
  Observe customs_scene at customs when not freed(party) "A long counter, a strongbox chained to the wall, and a window barred like a gaol's. Through a grille at the back a big man in a drover's cloak sits on a bench with his hands between his knees.".
  Observe customs_after at customs when freed(party) "A long counter and a strongbox chained to the wall. The grille at the back stands open on an empty bench.".
  Observe mardle_says at customs as sign when not freed(party) and not sent(party) and not knows(party, clerk_count) "'Forty head at the march-stone,' Mardle is saying to the customs-man, with a finger on the tally-book. 'Thirty-six in the pens. Four hidden from the Rì.'" teaches clerk_count.
  Observe pens_scene at pens when not freed(party) and not watered(party) and not halved(party) "Thirty-six black bullocks of the fells, rough-coated and restless, crowd the rails, bawling to be watered.".
  Observe pens_halved at pens when not freed(party) and halved(party) "Eighteen black bullocks are left at the rails. The other half of the pen is churned and empty.".
  Observe pens_watered at pens when not freed(party) and watered(party) and not halved(party) "Thirty-six black bullocks of the fells stand quiet at the rails, steaming, their trough full.".
  Observe owain_water near owain of owain when at(owain, pens) and not freed(party) "{owain} is carrying water to them a bucket at a time, in a cloak too big for him.".
  Observe owain_waits near owain of owain when at(owain, green) and not freed(party) "{owain} stands at the edge of the quay with his hands in his armpits, watching the customs-house door.".
  Observe pens_freed at pens when freed(party) and not sold(party) and not fined(party) "Bran is in among the bullocks, counting them again with a hand on each back.".
  Observe pens_after at pens when freed(party) and (sold(party) or fined(party)) "The pens are churned and empty. The drove has gone on to the sales.".
  // A sign, for anyone who looks, that something lies in the water to be searched for (CL-04: the search had sat in the
  // rest at the one place it mattered).
  Observe rhyne_sign at rhyne as sign when not knows(party, found_drowned) "Where the bank has slumped, something big and dark lies just under the black water, and the smell is worst there.".
  Observe rhyne_scene at rhyne when true "A dyke of black water between steep banks, the far bank slumped into it where the sea came over in the winter. The smell reaches you before the sight does.".

  Person clerk "Silas Mardle" at customs { Role "the Rì's customs clerk at Porthalen, who counts every beast that crosses the march". Pronouns he. Peaceable. Manner proud. }
  // Known to a company that came down with the drove (the drove road's origin: Owain its kin), not met as a stranger
  // (cold play 3, CL-26: Owain, "your cousin", and Bran had both greeted it as someone they had never seen).
  Person bran "Bran ap Ifor" at customs { Role "the Brynach lead-drover, held behind the customs-house grille". Pronouns he. Peaceable. Manner stoic.
    Greets "Bran looks up through the grille and knows you. 'You came,' he says. 'Good. Listen.'" when kin(party, owain). }
  Person owain "Owain" at green { Role "Bran's drover's boy, fourteen, who came down with the drove". Pronouns he. Peaceable.
    Greets "Owain is at your side at once. 'What do we do?' he asks." when kin(party, owain) and not freed(party).
    Greets "Owain is at your side at once. 'He's out,' he says, and grins." when kin(party, owain) and freed(party). }
  // Bran let out, the boy has his own way home to say (cold play 4's 11: "What do we do?" with nothing to answer).
  Topic owain_after with owain "Ask Owain what he will do now" when freed(party) once {
    Says "'Go home with Bran,' says {owain}. 'He sells them at the sales, and then it's four days up the drove road to Caer Brynach.' He looks at you, and then away. 'You could come. He said so.'".
  }
  // The boy waits on the landing for whoever will listen, and goes back to the beasts once someone has.
  Rule owain_to_pens when knows(party, boy_count) and at(owain, green) and not freed(party) and not sent(party) { Assert at(owain, pens). }
  Thing book "Mardle's tally-book" at customs {
    State shut "A tally-book bound in sheepskin lies open on the counter, under Mardle's hand.".
  }
  Discovery found_drowned "Four drowned bullocks lie in the Black Rhyne behind the pens, Brynach brands on their flanks." {
    Found by searching rhyne "Down where the bank has slumped, under the black water, something big and dark: a bullock, and another beyond it, four in all, the brand of a Brynach drove burnt into each flank. They have been there since last night.".
  }

  Topic clerk_count_t with clerk "Ask Mardle how many head crossed" when not knows(actor, found_drowned) and not freed(party) and not sent(party) once {
    Says "Mardle turns the tally-book so you can see it, and lays a finger on the line. 'Forty head at the march-stone. I counted them myself, at dawn. Thirty-six in the pens. The Rì's law is the Rì's law: four hidden beasts, a fine of twelve crowns, or the man stays where he is.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, clerk_count). }
  }
  Topic bran_count_t with bran "Ask Bran what happened" when not freed(party) once {
    Says "Bran looks up slowly. 'Thirty-six crossed. Four went into the Black Rhyne behind the pens, when the bank gave under them. Ask the boy. And I'd pay the tenth on thirty-six without a word if it were the Rì's tenth.' He looks past you at the counter. 'It is not the Rì's. Ask how many droves Mardle has found four short this year.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, bran_count). }
  }
  Topic owain_count_t with owain "Ask Owain how many head came down" when not freed(party) once {
    Says "'Thirty-six,' says {owain} at once, and then, because you are listening: 'There were forty at Hafod. At the Black Rhyne the bank went from under the last of them, in the dark. We heard them in the water. Bran said leave them, or we'd lose the rest.' He points with his chin, behind the pens. 'They're still there.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, boy_count). }
  }
  Topic keeper_drove with keeper "Ask {keeper} about the drover the customs-men hold" when not freed(party) once {
    Says "{keeper} lowers their voice. 'Third drove this year Mardle has found four short. The reeve takes his word: he keeps the Rì's book, and she has the sea-gate to think of. Nobody here will cross him. Nobody here sells cattle.'".
  }
  // Mardle shows the line himself (clerk_count_t), so what can fail is seeing what is wrong with it, not reading it
  // (cold play 3, CL-27: the book turned to be read, then a look at it failed).
  Action read_book(actor: group, site: place) "Look closely at the ink on Bran's line" {
    Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, customs) and knows(actor, clerk_count)
      and not knows(actor, altered) and not knows(actor, found_drowned) and not freed(actor) and not sent(actor) and not counted(actor).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, altered). Assert counted(actor). }
    On failure { Assert counted(actor). }
    Result "The line for Bran's drove reads forty, in a good round hand. But the ink of the four is blacker than the ink of the rest, and under it, where the nib scratched, is the tail of a three and the curl of a six.".
    Otherwise "The line reads forty, in a good round hand. You see nothing wrong with it before Mardle closes the book. 'The Rì's book, friend.'".
  }
  // Bran's lead put to the man it is about (CL-27: "ask how many droves Mardle has found four short" had no topic).
  Topic clerk_short_t with clerk "Ask Mardle how many droves he has found four short this year" when knows(actor, bran_count) and not knows(actor, altered) and not freed(party) and not sent(party) once {
    Says "'Every drove that was four short,' says Mardle. His finger stays on the line in the book, and he does not look at you.".
  }
  Topic pay_fine with clerk "Pay Mardle the twelve crowns, and have Bran let out" when not freed(party) and not sent(party) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 12 once {
    Says "Mardle counts the coins twice and writes in the book. The grille opens. Bran comes out stooping, straightens, and looks at Mardle a long moment before he looks at you. 'He'll do it to the next drove,' he says.".
    On discuss {
      Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 12. Assert freed(actor). Assert fined(actor). Assert knows(actor, road_west).
      Assert knows(actor, mardle_paid).
    }
  }
  Action show_drowned(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Mardle where the four bullocks are" {
    Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, customs) and knows(actor, found_drowned) and not freed(party) and not sent(party).
    Result "Mardle's mouth thins. 'Beasts in a ditch prove nothing to the Rì's book.' But the customs-man at the door has heard, and goes out to look, and comes back, and says something low. Mardle shuts the book. 'Let him out,' he says. 'And tell the reeve nothing she need be troubled with.'".
    On success { Assert freed(actor). Assert knows(actor, road_west). }
  }
  Action show_altered(actor: group, site: place) "Tell Mardle you saw what is under the forty" {
    Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, customs) and knows(actor, altered) and not freed(party) and not sent(party).
    Result "For a moment Mardle does nothing at all. Then he takes a key from his belt and unlocks the grille himself, and does not look at you while he does it. 'A clerk's slip,' he says to the counter. By evening the whole of the waterfront has heard which clerk, and whose slip.".
    On success {
      Assert freed(actor). Assert turned(clerk). Assert knows(actor, road_west). Assert knows(actor, mardle_shown).
    }
  }
  // Let out, Bran says his thanks and where he is going himself, at once: the second cold play had him leave without
  // a word, his thanks behind a question nobody thought to ask (CL-03).
  Rule bran_thanks when freed(party) and not thanked(party) says "'Now I sell them, and drink, and go home,' says Bran. 'Up the drove road to Caer Brynach, four days with an empty drove.' He grips your hand like a gate-post. 'Come up the pass. There's work in Brynach for anyone who'll stand by a drover, and the lord pays for a sword: something has been at the cattle on the high pasture. Say Bran ap Ifor sent you.'" teaches road_west { Assert thanked(party). }

  Rule bran_out when freed(party) and at(bran, customs) { Assert at(bran, pens). }
  // What was done answered where it was done (Sprint 2, S2-5; cold play 4: Bran's "sell, drink, go home" went
  // nowhere, the drove dropped out of the story, and nothing at the landing knew the drover was out): the drove taken
  // to the sales with him, his share for the four found; the landing heard of it; the road west said as his own.
  Action drive_to_sales(actor: group, site: place) "Help Bran take the drove to the sales" {
    Time 1 hours.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pens) and at(bran, pens) and freed(actor)
      and not fined(actor) and not sold(actor).
    Result "Thirty-six bullocks through the lanes to the sale-yard, Owain at the back with a stick. They go at a good price. Bran pays you out of it in the yard: four coin. 'For the four you found,' he says." when not halved(actor).
    Result "Eighteen bullocks through the lanes to the sale-yard, Owain at the back with a stick. Bran says nothing of the other eighteen. He pays you out of what they bring: two coin. 'It should have been four,' he says." when halved(actor).
    On success { Assert sold(actor). }
  }
  // How Bran was got out, as a fact the sea-gate reads (ST-04: the smugglers pay Mardle one sack in ten): shown up, he
  // can protect nobody; paid off, he is at the counter still, and warns his friends the company is about.
  Entity mardle_shown: fact "Mardle the customs clerk was shown up at his own counter, and is gone from {town}.".
  Entity mardle_paid: fact "Mardle the customs clerk was paid his twelve crowns, and keeps the counter at {town}.".
  Rule share_whole when sold(party) and not halved(party) and not paid(party) { Assert paid(party). Increase quantity(party, gold) by 4. }
  Rule share_half when sold(party) and halved(party) and not paid(party) { Assert paid(party). Increase quantity(party, gold) by 2. }
  // Mardle sells the drove himself, on a clock of his own (the owner's structural critique, 18 November, ST-02: a
  // deadline had been the only actor): the sale cried, a buyer at the pens, half the drove under the hammer.
  Rule sale_cried when not freed(party) and not sent(party) and not cried(party) and watch(clock) >= 60 says "A customs-man nails a paper to the customs-house door: Bran ap Ifor's drove to be sold at the pens on the third day, for the Rì's toll." { Assert cried(party). }
  Rule buyer_comes when not freed(party) and not sent(party) and cried(party) and not bidden(party) and watch(clock) >= 162 says "A buyer from Wrackham walks the rails at the pens with Mardle, pointing with his stick. Owain stands in the gate and will not move out of it until Mardle tells him to." { Assert bidden(party). }
  Rule half_sold when not freed(party) and not sent(party) and bidden(party) and not halved(party) and watch(clock) >= 312 says "The sale begins at the pens. Eighteen of Bran's bullocks go under the hammer to the Wrackham man before Mardle calls a halt for the day." { Assert halved(party). }
  // What Mardle is afraid of, said where he is pressed (ST-02: obstruction had stood where a claim should).
  Topic clerk_fear with clerk "Ask Mardle who he counts for" when knows(actor, bran_count) and not freed(party) once {
    Says "'For the toll-farmer at Dun Rìerdan,' says Mardle. 'He docks me a crown for every beast that comes in short of what the march-stone saw, and he does not ask why. I have three children in the house behind the chandlery.' He closes the book. 'Count for him a year, and see if you count kinder.'".
  }
  // What each way of getting Bran out leaves behind (ST-02's aftermath): shown up by the ink, Mardle is gone, and his
  // family with him; bought out, he is at the counter for the next drove.
  Rule mardle_gone when turned(clerk) and at(party, green) and not gone(party) says "On the quay, a woman you have not seen before is loading a handcart outside the house behind the chandlery: bedding, a chair, a box of pots. Three children sit on the box. Nobody on the waterfront helps her, and nobody stops her." { Assert gone(party). }
  Topic keeper_after with keeper "Ask {keeper} what the waterfront is saying" when freed(party) once {
    Says "'That you got the Brynach drover out from under Mardle,' says {keeper}, and puts a loaf on the counter and pushes it across. 'For the road.'".
    On discuss { Increase quantity(actor, rations) by 1. Assert heard(actor). }
  }
  Rule heard_kept when heard(party) and not fined(party) and not turned(clerk) and not told(party) says "'Third drove this year he's had four short of. Nobody here would cross him.'" { Assert told(party). }
  Rule heard_paid when heard(party) and fined(party) and not told(party) says "{keeper} does not quite look at you. 'Paid him his twelve crowns, they say. He'll be at the counter for the next drove, then.'" { Assert told(party). }
  Rule heard_gone when heard(party) and turned(clerk) and not told(party) says "'And that Mardle's gone, out of the town by tonight, his wife and the children with him. Half the waterfront will drink to you, and the other half will remember it was you.'" { Assert told(party). }
  Topic bran_west with bran "Ask Bran about the work in Brynach" when freed(party) and (sold(party) or fined(party)) once {
    Says "'The old road west,' says Bran, 'past the march-stone and up the pass. Four days to Caer Brynach.' He points with his whole arm, the way a drover does. 'Something takes the beasts off the high pasture at night, and leaves nothing. The lord pays a sword. Ask for me.'".
  }
  Rule owain_goes when freed(party) and at(owain, pens) { Assert at(owain, green). }

  Milestone m_freed "saw Bran ap Ifor let out of the customs-house" worth 150 when freed(party).
  Milestone m_turned "showed what was under the clerk's forty" worth 100 when turned(clerk).
  Objective held_aim when not sent(party) and knows(party, held) and not freed(party) and not knows(party, boy_count) and not knows(party, found_drowned) and not knows(party, altered) toward owain by pens "Ask Owain how many head came down: the customs clerk says four were hidden from the toll.".
  Action water_drove(actor: group, site: place) "Water the drove from the pens' trough" {
    Time 1 hours.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, pens) and not watered(actor) and not freed(actor) and not sent(actor).
    Result "Bucket after bucket from the trough, until your arms go and the bawling stops. The bullocks stand steaming and quiet at the rails, and the boy says something that might be thanks.".
    On success { Assert watered(actor). }
  }
  Objective held_rhyne when not sent(party) and knows(party, boy_count) and not knows(party, found_drowned) and not knows(party, altered) and not freed(party) toward rhyne by pens "Search the Black Rhyne behind the pens for the four that went in.".
  Objective held_proof when not sent(party) and (knows(party, found_drowned) or knows(party, altered)) and not freed(party) toward customs "Tell Mardle at the customs-house what you found, and have Bran let out.".
  // The inquiry is the thread followed first; minding the drove and hearing Bran stand beside it (the second cold
  // play: with the drove first, the search of the rhyne was never led, CL-04).
  // Bran is to be heard behind the grille, said from the first beside the boy's count; the drove is watered at the
  // pens, offered there (an aim of its own had taken the thread from the inquiry: CL-04).
  Objective bran_aim when not sent(party) and knows(party, held) and not freed(party) and not knows(party, bran_count) toward customs "Go to Bran behind the customs-house grille, and hear what he says of the count.".
  // The clock: four days, and the customs-men send a man who will not pay north to the Judges, and sell his drove.
  Rule sent_north when not freed(party) and not sent(party) and watch(clock) >= 576 says "Word comes along the waterfront: the customs-men have sent Bran ap Ifor north to the Judges in chains, and sold his drove at the sales for the Rì's toll." {
    Assert sent(party). Assert stale(held). Retract at(bran, customs). Assert offstage(bran). Assert at(owain, green).
  }
  Rule word_old when freed(party) and not stale(held) { Assert stale(held). }
  Goal freed(party).
}
